WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.215 --> 00:00:00.840
RETO MEIER: Hi.

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.150
I'm Reto Meier, Google
Developer Advocate.

00:00:03.150 --> 00:00:06.240
Today I learned that every
car crash, 311 call, tree,

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.030
Citi Bike trip and station, and
limousine ride in New York City

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:12.116
is available as public data
sets in Google BigQuery.

00:00:12.116 --> 00:00:14.060
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:17.790
Do you know on which
New York City streets

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:20.310
you're most likely to find
a loud party, maybe the one

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:22.920
place where a collision caused
by an animal also injured

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.190
a cyclist, or the Citi Bike
record for the longest distance

00:00:26.190 --> 00:00:28.230
ridden in the shortest time?

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:30.480
One of the amazing things
about working at Google

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.450
is the ability to do whatever's
necessary to find answers.

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:40.260
So let's head to New
York-- or to this computer

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.122
representation of New York
from here in San Francisco.

00:00:44.122 --> 00:00:45.580
After all, what
better way is there

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:47.910
to get to know New York City
than by immersing yourself

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:51.720
in the hustle and bustle of
data analysis and visualizations

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:54.500
representing its 8.5
million residents and 50

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:56.370
million yearly visitors?

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:58.710
For example, in 2016
these city streets

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:01.140
witnessed a lot of
traffic accidents.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.660
There were over 200,000
motor vehicle collisions

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:05.280
across the five
boroughs, resulting

00:01:05.280 --> 00:01:09.030
in over 50,000 injuries
and 200 deaths,

00:01:09.030 --> 00:01:11.700
mainly due to driver
inattention and motorcyclists

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:14.755
being the most likely to die
in the case of a collision.

00:01:14.755 --> 00:01:16.380
When the temperature
in New York drops,

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:19.020
New Yorkers retreat
inside and call 311

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:21.700
about the snow or lack
of heat and hot water,

00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:23.522
especially in the Bronx.

00:01:23.522 --> 00:01:25.230
All across New York,
people are concerned

00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:28.080
with the noise and the
condition of the city streets.

00:01:28.080 --> 00:01:29.550
But when you
normalize the results

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:31.784
by the size of each
borough's population,

00:01:31.784 --> 00:01:33.450
you see that the
people of Staten Island

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:35.880
have the biggest
infrastructure issues.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.640
No matter the weather, it's the
potholes, rough, cracked roads,

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:41.930
and cave-ins that have
Staten Islanders calling 311.

00:01:41.930 --> 00:01:43.920
If it's a Wednesday,
the people of New York

00:01:43.920 --> 00:01:47.700
are taking lots of short
rides on their Citi Bikes.

00:01:47.700 --> 00:01:51.840
Since 2013, there's been over
33 million Citi Bike rides

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:54.190
averaging 15 minutes per ride.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:57.780
Riders skew 76%
men to 24% women,

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:02.550
and with 52% of all riders
aged between 27 and 41,

00:02:02.550 --> 00:02:06.630
with this route alongside the
Hudson by far the most popular.

00:02:06.630 --> 00:02:08.530
Using these preloaded
public data sets,

00:02:08.530 --> 00:02:11.670
you can investigate almost
every aspect of the city.

00:02:11.670 --> 00:02:15.510
By analyzing tree survey data,
you can discover that, in 1995,

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:18.840
the most common tree in
New York was the Norway

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:23.790
maple with over 100,000
trees and that, by 2005, it

00:02:23.790 --> 00:02:26.880
was overtaken by the
London planetree.

